{"quote_id":"FL-CUR-003","corpus_id":"S001","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Five Lessons (Master Class)","source_year":1948,"source_slug":"five_lessons","source_section":"Lesson 1","quote_original":"When satisfaction is yours, you no longer hunger for it.","primary_topic":"WISH_FULFILLED","secondary_topics":["FEELING"],"tags":["satisfaction","desire","completion"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_five_lessons.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FL-CUR-005","corpus_id":"S001","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Five Lessons (Master Class)","source_year":1948,"source_slug":"five_lessons","source_section":"Lesson 1","quote_original":"The first step in changing the future is Desire, that is, define your objective — know definitely what you want.","primary_topic":"DESIRE","secondary_topics":["TECHNIQUE"],"tags":["desire","objective","clarity"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_five_lessons.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FL-CUR-006","corpus_id":"S001","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Five Lessons (Master Class)","source_year":1948,"source_slug":"five_lessons","source_section":"Lesson 1","quote_original":"Experience has taught me to restrict the imaginary action which implies fulfillment of the desire, to condense the idea into a single act, and to re-enact it over and over again until it has the feeling of reality.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","secondary_topics":["TECHNIQUE","FEELING"],"tags":["imaginal-act","repetition","feeling-of-reality"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_five_lessons.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FL-CUR-007","corpus_id":"S001","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Five Lessons (Master Class)","source_year":1948,"source_slug":"five_lessons","source_section":"Lesson 1","quote_original":"You must, with the minimum of effort permeate the mind with the feeling of the wish fulfilled.","primary_topic":"WISH_FULFILLED","secondary_topics":["EFFORT"],"tags":["minimum-effort","feeling","wish-fulfilled"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_five_lessons.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FL-CUR-028","corpus_id":"S001","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Five Lessons (Master Class)","source_year":1948,"source_slug":"five_lessons","source_section":"Lesson 1","quote_original":"You must participate in the imaginary action, not merely stand back and look on, but FEEL that you are actually performing the action, so that the imaginary sensation is real to you.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","secondary_topics":["FEELING","TECHNIQUE"],"tags":["participation","imaginal-act","feeling"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_five_lessons.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FL-CUR-009","corpus_id":"S001","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Five Lessons (Master Class)","source_year":1948,"source_slug":"five_lessons","source_section":"Lesson 2","quote_original":"Just relax and enter into the feeling of actually being what you want to be.","primary_topic":"FEELING","secondary_topics":["SELF_CONCEPT"],"tags":["relaxation","identity","desire"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_five_lessons.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FL-CUR-029","corpus_id":"S001","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Five Lessons (Master Class)","source_year":1948,"source_slug":"five_lessons","source_section":"Lesson 2","quote_original":"There is all the difference in the world between holding the idea, and being held by the idea.","primary_topic":"ATTENTION","secondary_topics":["PERSISTENCE"],"tags":["idea","attention","persistence"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_five_lessons.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FL-CUR-030","corpus_id":"S001","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Five Lessons (Master Class)","source_year":1948,"source_slug":"five_lessons","source_section":"Lesson 2","quote_original":"Use wisely the interval preceding sleep. Assume the feeling of the wish fulfilled and go to sleep in this mood.","primary_topic":"SLEEP_SATS","secondary_topics":["WISH_FULFILLED","FEELING"],"tags":["sleep","mood","wish-fulfilled"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_five_lessons.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FL-CUR-031","corpus_id":"S001","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Five Lessons (Master Class)","source_year":1948,"source_slug":"five_lessons","source_section":"Lesson 2","quote_original":"Know what you want. Then construct a single event, an event which implies fulfillment of your wish. Restrict the event to a single act.","primary_topic":"TECHNIQUE","secondary_topics":["DESIRE","IMAGINATION"],"tags":["objective","single-event","imaginal-act"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_five_lessons.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FL-CUR-032","corpus_id":"S001","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Five Lessons (Master Class)","source_year":1948,"source_slug":"five_lessons","source_section":"Lesson 3","quote_original":"Take my challenge and put this philosophy to the test. If it does not work you should not use it as a comforter.","primary_topic":"PRACTICE","secondary_topics":["TESTING"],"tags":["practice","test","experience"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_five_lessons.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FL-CUR-016","corpus_id":"S001","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Five Lessons (Master Class)","source_year":1948,"source_slug":"five_lessons","source_section":"Lesson 4","quote_original":"To know what you want is the start of prayer.","primary_topic":"DESIRE","secondary_topics":["PRAYER"],"tags":["clarity","prayer","desire"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_five_lessons.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FL-CUR-018","corpus_id":"S001","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Five Lessons (Master Class)","source_year":1948,"source_slug":"five_lessons","source_section":"Lesson 4","quote_original":"What would I feel like, now, were I what I want to be?","primary_topic":"FEELING","secondary_topics":["SELF_CONCEPT"],"tags":["feeling","identity","question"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_five_lessons.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FL-CUR-020","corpus_id":"S001","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Five Lessons (Master Class)","source_year":1948,"source_slug":"five_lessons","source_section":"Lesson 5","quote_original":"Give yourself a new concept of self for the old concept. Give up the old concept completely.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","secondary_topics":["CHANGE"],"tags":["self-concept","change","release"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_five_lessons.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
